# Material UI

## Imports
```typescript
// Use single line imports for Material UI components
import { Button, Stack } from '@mui/material';
```

## Typography
- Use Typography variants instead of fontFamily key in sxProps objects
- Use Typography variants instead of direct font styling
- Match typography variants from Figma with the existing file content /shared/theme/baseTheme/typography.ts

## Modals
- Use @ebay/nice-modal-react approach for modal management

## SxProps usage
- Use external objects for sx props instead of inline styles
- Use full written css-in-js keys (paddingTop instead of pt, etc.) instead of abbreviated
- Use only variant prop for Button components

### Use sxProps in a separate styles object next to the component
```typescript
// Component with sxProps usage
const styles = {
  root: {
    color: 'primary.main',
  },
} satisfies sxProps;

const MyComponent = () => {
  return <Box sx={styles.root}></Box>;
}
```

### Use mui-sx library for styles composition
```typescript
import muiSx from 'mui-sx';
…
<Slider sx={muiSx({ styles.slider, { sx: styles.sliderActive, condition: isActive } )} } />
```

### Use px instead of spacing
```typescript
// Set values in pixels for consistent sizing
const styles = {
  box: {
    width: '24px',
    height: '10px',
  },
} satisfies SxProps;
```

## Theme usage

### Use colors from palette
```typescript
// Use theme palette colors for consistent theming
const styles = {
  box: {
    color: 'success.main',
  },
} satisfies SxProps;
```

### Use media queries breakpoints in a properly way
```typescript
const styles = {
  box: {
    width: {
      sx: '100%',
      md: '280px',
    },
  },
} satisfies SxProps;
```

### Use z-index only from the theme values
```typescript
// Use theme-defined z-index values for consistent layering
const styles = {
  box: {
    zIndex: 'tooltip',
  },
} satisfies SxProps;
```